WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.160
The cultist screamed.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:09.960
The long and spindly but unimaginably powerful
arm of the Shy Guy had him by the leg, dragging

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.280
him backwards, his fingernails carving deep
ruts into the floor.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:20.400
His friend was already on the run, but his
death warrant had been sealed by a glance.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.180
In the history of evil plans, rarely has an
evil plan backfired so spectacularly.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:33.060
As the Shy Guy bellowed, destroying its latest
prey and galloping after the second, which

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:39.120
would soon become the third, and the fourth,
and the fifth, and so much more as the personnel

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.500
of the SCP Foundation caught unplanned glimpses
of his terrible face.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.300
it would take a God to undo the chaos that
was unfolding.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:54.360
The exact same God that these two idiot cultists
were here to destroy.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.280
The plan had seemed so simple, so perfectly
straightforward on paper.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.620
Sneak into the SCP Foundation and assassinate
SCP-343.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.860
That being said, even deluded cultists of
the Scarlet King knew that killing the anomaly

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:16.020
believed to be God himself was going to be
far easier in theory than in practice.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.900
And yet, neither one of this intrepid pair
of Foundation impersonators could ever have

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.660
predicted things would go this bad.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:30.300
Several years earlier, Zachary and Cash, were
nothing more than a pair of social shut-ins

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.040
trawling forums on the internet from the secluded
sanctuary of their basements.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.560
In fact, it was on a particular one of these
forums that would lead to the pair eventually

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.460
meeting in person: Parawatch, a deep-web online
space for discussions of the supernatural.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:53.040
While there was nothing inherently insidious
about Parawatch itself, it did draw in those

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.740
who were interested in the paranormal and
even the anomalous, like Zach and Cash.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:04.500
And that made the forum the perfect recruitment
tool for those whose intentions were far more

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.460
nefarious.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.920
Both men were individually approached by another
user, who was only known by his screen name

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.960
‘C.ot.S.K’.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:19.020
Over some lengthy conversations with this
mysterious third party, both Zach and Cash

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:25.080
found themselves being convinced into believing
the core tenets of a murderous cult that revered

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.920
a conceptual deity: the Children of the Scarlet
King.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.500
And it was during a secret gathering of their
fellow members that Cash and Zach would not

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.600
only meet, but find themselves specifically
tasked with a mission that was meant to clear

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.020
the way for the Scarlet King to enter our
reality.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:48.000
Simply put, the two of them were tasked with
killing God.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.460
The plan was devised by one of the longer-standing
Children of the Scarlet King, who divulged

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.860
their cult’s knowledge of the SCP Foundation.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:02.880
Specifically, an entity known as SCP-343,
a powerful reality warper who had claimed

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.580
to be the architect of the very universe itself.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:11.520
In the eyes of the Scarlet King’s followers,
this meant that SCP-343 could pose a direct

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.580
threat to the ascension of their destructive
deity.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.740
If the Scarlet King was ever to gain access
to this universe, there was a high chance

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.620
SCP-343 could oppose him.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.320
So, with stolen credentials and Foundation
personnel garb, Zach and Cash were sent in

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.640
to ‘remove’ SCP-343 from the equation.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.100
It goes without saying that killing a being
believed to be God himself was hardly an easy

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.300
goal to achieve.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:46.020
Nobody could just poison SCP-343, or take
him out using conventional weapons, or even

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.400
use any other typical methods of assassination
that would work on a human target.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.420
Instead, Zach and Cash needed to get creative.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:04:00.000
Luckily, there was another anomaly kept contained
by the SCP Foundation that the Children of

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.240
the Scarlet King had thought would be perfect
for the job.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:09.540
It was a Miniature Event Horizon, a black
sphere that could pull any nearby matter into

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.140
itself.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.000
Anything brought within the vicinity of this
anomalous wormhole would quickly be sucked

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.840
in, and ultimately lost forever with no chance
of retrieval.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:24.720
Sure, it might not kill SCP-343, strictly
speaking, but it could certainly remove him

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.700
from play, leaving the universe unprotected
against the rise of the Scarlet King.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.760
However, there was one tiny problem…

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:39.900
one otherwise minute detail that, because
it went uncorrected, jeopardized the whole

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:40.440
plan.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.480
It could have been down to inaccurate information
that the Children of the Scarlet King had

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.980
on the SCP Foundation.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:53.040
After all, the organization was known for
keeping its operations and even its very existence

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.780
a closely guarded secret.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:05:00.900
Or perhaps, sheerly due to human error, the
wrong number was said by the wrong cultist

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:07.860
at the wrong moment, misheard or misread leading
to a ‘4’ being replaced with a ‘6’.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.220
You see, the Miniature&nbsp;
Event Horizon was designated&nbsp;

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.900
as SCP-094, but by mistake, Zach and Cash

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:23.820
had slipped undetected into the Foundation
in search of SCP-096, unaware that anomaly

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.040
was far from what they were expecting.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:31.140
The look of terror on Zach’s face appeared
instantly as the pair of Scarlet King fanatics

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.060
opened the door to the containment cell.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:39.720
That same horrified look had vanished just
as quickly the second that SCP-096 took notice

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.220
of the two visitors.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.160
In the blink of an eye,&nbsp;
the abnormally proportioned&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.500
humanoid anomaly had gone from being hunched

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.900
over in a corner, gently rocking itself, to
standing directly in front of Zach and Cash,

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:56.040
towering over them both and&nbsp;
screeching incoherently.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:01.500
Cash turned and ran, abandoning his cultist
compatriot as Zach screamed in fear.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.240
The Shy Guy had grabbed him.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:09.180
A moment later, his screams had been silenced,
thanks to SCP-096.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.760
Cash had no idea what the creature was – all
he knew was it certainly wasn’t the miniaturized

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:17.340
black hole he and Zach had been sent to find.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.740
But he tried to keep the original goal in
mind even in a moment of crisis: take out

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.580
SCP-343 so the Scarlet King could rise.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:32.220
Maybe this other anomaly, whatever it was,
could stand a chance against the reality warper.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:37.440
Cash would never get to find out, however,
as he was tackled to the group by a Foundation

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.020
security team as he turned a corner.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:46.380
But SCP-096 had been hot on the cultist’s
heels, and had appeared behind him just as

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.020
he was being restrained by security officers.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:55.260
And the whole unit could see the Shy Guy now…
which meant not one of them stood a chance.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:59.880
Meanwhile, elsewhere in the facility, oblivious
to the carnage of the unfolding containment

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:06.420
beach, SCP-343 was enjoying a stroll around
the Foundation site, with a hamburger in one

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:08.340
hand and a milkshake in the other.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:13.380
He’d spent most of the afternoon the way
he usually did, phasing out of reality to

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:18.000
an extradimensional astral plane outside of
the known universe where he could privately

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.140
enjoy a game of Solitaire using a deck of
cards conjured out of nothingness.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:27.240
Upon returning, polishing off the dregs of
his lunch, which he’d also willed into existence

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:32.880
from nowhere, SCP-343 barely noticed that
the entire Foundation seemed to be on red

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:33.300
alert.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:37.920
Or, more accurately, he did notice, he just
didn’t do much to help.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:43.620
You see, one of the more notable things about
SCP-343 – aside from the fact that he can

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:48.360
use his anomalous abilities to do literally
anything imaginable – is that he very much

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.520
enjoys taking a back seat.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:55.440
He claims that, after creating the universe,
he got tired of having to be in control of

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.600
everything, everywhere, all at once.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:05.520
And so, while SCP-343 could right every wrong
and solve every problem in the entire universe,

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:11.580
he chooses not to, all to pursue the illusion
of giving up control and leaving the universe

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:12.660
to its own devices.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:19.020
That is, unless something tries to harm him
directly… and something was very much about

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:19.380
to.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:24.840
While the pair of Scarlet King cultists who
had accidentally set SCP-096 free were already

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:28.500
dead, they’d unknowingly started a chain
reaction.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.940
The Foundation desperately dispatched more
of its personnel to try and re-contain the

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:37.080
Shy Guy, but the more they sent, the more
of them observed the creature.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:41.880
This gave SCP-096 even more targets, extending&nbsp;

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:44.100
its rage state as it zipped&nbsp;
through the Foundation,

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.160
killing everyone that had clapped eyes on
it.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.700
Until that rage-fuelled&nbsp;
rampage led to coincidentally&nbsp;

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.660
cross paths with SCP-343, who had just walked

00:08:54.660 --> 00:09:00.600
through a wall on his way back to his cell…
right into the path of SCP-096.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:08.100
“Oh dear, dear me,” SCP-343 sighed, finishing
the remainder of his milkshake before making

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.960
the empty cup and straw disappear.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.020
“It’s been some time, hasn’t it, Ian?

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.480
My boy, look at what’s become of you.”

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:22.740
For a moment, SCP-096 seemed to pause, its
pale skin flecked with droplets of blood thanks

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:27.120
to the sheer number of guards and researchers
it had torn through for daring to look at

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:27.240
it.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:32.280
“I see you’re still having the same old
troubles,” the reality warper continued,

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:36.600
reacting eerily, calmly, and casually towards
the towering monster.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:40.200
“You know, you really ought to work on your
confidence.”

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.700
That did it.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:46.980
The sentence touched a nerve within the Shy
Guy, giving it a pang of sadness that erupted

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.320
quickly into an unbridled rage.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:55.380
It didn’t matter that SCP-343 was a powerful
anomaly with the ability to do almost anything:

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:00.960
he had still looked at SCP-096, in fact, he
was looking directly at it.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.360
And that meant he had to go.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:09.300
His fate was sealed, as the creature began
wailing and charged straight for SCP-343.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:15.780
With a casual wave of his hand, God swiped
the creature aside, sending SCP-096 flying.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:20.520
Thrown telekinetically – much to its surprise
– the creature found itself phasing through

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:24.120
walls as it sailed between corridors and other
containment chambers.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:31.080
In and out, in and out until it sailed through
the solid steel wall of its own cell, landing

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.720
right back in the corner that it had started
in.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:40.440
But rather than return to crying in a fetal
position as it normally did, SCP-096 got right

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:46.260
back up and raced back through the halls of
the facility, homing in on SCP-343.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:51.180
Being sent back to its room was enough to
keep the Shy Guy’s rage state active, and

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:56.460
it hadn’t changed the fact that God had
still looked at it, so he had to kill him.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:03.780
Traveling at anomalous speeds, SCP-096 blinked
into existence right behind SCP-343 as he

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.000
sat down and relaxed in his favorite chair.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.820
The horrific humanoid shrieked loudly, although
SCP-343 didn’t turn around to look at it;

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.800
he already knew it was there.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:17.010
He had sensed it even before it left its cell.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:22.320
With yet another lazy swish of his hand, SCP-343
sent the Shy Guy away.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:28.740
This time, SCP-096 realized its long legs
seemed to be moving independently, walking

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:34.680
backwards along the exact same steps it had
taken to get into SCP-343’s containment

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:35.160
chamber.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:40.080
It continued going backwards, and despite
its frustrated attempts to rush back towards

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.420
the reality-warping old man, it couldn’t.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:45.900
Little did the Shy Guy realize it wasn’t
the only one.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:52.800
SCP-343’s command over the fundamental laws
of the universe was so great that he had altered

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:53.760
time itself.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:59.760
Everything was now running in reverse, albeit
for a few short moments; birds in the sky

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:05.160
were flying backwards, waterfalls were flowing
upwards, the Earth was spinning in the opposite

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.600
direction on its axis.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:14.280
Everything in existence was like an old VCR
tape being rewound, until SCP-096 found itself

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.980
once again back in its cell.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:20.760
Now the Shy Guy was mad; really, really mad.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:26.700
The moment SCP-343 allowed time to return
to its normal, forward chronological flow,

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:32.760
SCP-096 once again raced out of its containment
chamber, hunting down the latest person to

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.500
have seen its wide-jawed face.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:40.680
Usually, nothing could stop SCP-096 from catching
up to its target, often killing them without

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.160
fail.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:46.740
But the fact that SCP-343 could so easily
rework the rules of the universe to send it

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:50.580
back to its room made the self-conscious creature
all the more agitated.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.400
And it was only going to get worse and worse.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:57.420
SCP-096 kept trying, infamously relentless.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:03.720
But every time, SCP-343 presented some new,
unpredictable way of stopping the Shy Guy

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.740
from getting to him.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:09.720
On one attempt, he caused the creature’s
atoms to rearrange themselves into long strands

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:13.920
the closer it got, effectively turning it
into Shy Guy spaghetti.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:19.800
During another, SCP-343 actually reworked
the way that sight works across the entire

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:24.660
universe, making it so that on a conceptual
level, he’d technically never looked at

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:29.400
SCP-096 according to this newly redefined
way of seeing things.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:34.800
Every time, SCP-343 set the Shy Guy back,
but never deterred him.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.920
He kept coming back, that is until…

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:45.360
Bored by the constant back and forth between
them, SCP-343 waited for SCP-096 to arrive

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:46.440
next to him once again.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:51.360
At that moment, he snapped his fingers, and
the creature stopped in its tracks.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:55.440
A story filled its mind, the story of a once
normal kid.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:14:01.440
This young child had been bullied and ostracised
by other children, made fun of for his appearance.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:06.420
They became depressed, self-loathing, keeping
away from everyone out of the fear they’d

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:07.020
been taunted.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:12.060
The child started to hide their face, desperate
that nobody look at them and laugh.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:16.260
“Listen,” SCP-343 told SCP-096.

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:21.420
There was nothing around them; the universe
had seemingly faded away as the pair stood

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.060
in a pocket of space outside of reality.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.220
“Just listen closely.”

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.360
Silence.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.200
Not a whisper, not even the creature’s own
breathing could be heard.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:37.080
“No-one’s laughing at you anymore,”
SCP-343 whispered.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.960
“It’s okay, you can stop now.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.480
There’s nobody left who can hurt you.”

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:47.820
With that, SCP-096’s very reason for being
had ceased.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:51.180
The Shy Guy didn’t exist anymore, it didn’t
need to.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:56.940
Restoring the universe to its previous state
with another click of his fingers, SCP-343

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.280
was free to sit back in his chair and relax.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:03.840
There he could continue pretending he wasn’t
in control…

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:11.040
Now go and check out “SCP-343 GOD VS BILL
CIPHER FROM GRAVITY FALLS” and “SCP-096

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.440
TALE A LESSON IN POWER” for more!

